# SYNTHETIC / DERIVED fixture. Not a captured sweep.
#
# Built for the query tests that need 'an old-scheme run and a new-scheme run
# of the same endpoints coexisting in one store', which no single real sweep
# can provide: after stage 1c-b3 the prober only ever writes the new subject
# scheme, so a run in the old scheme can no longer be captured live. This is
# the FIRST fixture in the derived-subject scheme (see prober/src/emit.rs's
# `subject_iri` and its `the_encoding_is_exactly_this` test for the exact
# shape pinned below); every other committed fixture, including
# run-with-samples.nq, still carries the old row-index scheme.
#
# Construction: the full real run from run-with-samples.nq (run
# 2026-08-22T16:00:00Z) is copied, with:
#
#   1. Every occurrence of 2026-08-22T16:00:00Z rewritten to
#      2026-08-22T20:00:00Z (a LATER sweep of the same three endpoints), so
#      this run is the most recent of the two wherever both are loaded.
#   2. Every `urn:sparqlwatch:measurement:<run>:<row index>` and
#      `urn:sparqlwatch:content-sample:<run>:<row index>` subject rewritten to
#      `urn:sparqlwatch:<kind>:<run>:<percent-encoded endpoint>:<metric id>`,
#      using prober/src/emit.rs's `encode_unreserved` exactly: RFC 3986's
#      unreserved set passed through unescaped, every other byte of the
#      endpoint's UTF-8 encoding as `%` plus two uppercase hex digits. No
#      `sw:NotMeasured` fact exists in run-with-samples.nq (it was captured
#      with --max-cost expensive), so this fixture has none either.
#
# Two further hand edits on top of the mechanical rewrite, exactly as
# run-two-sweeps.nq makes one hand edit for its own most-recent-run test:
#
#   3. Kadaster's sw:metric:classes dqv:value in this (20:00) run was changed
#      from "verified" (the value the mechanical copy would have produced,
#      matching the 16:00 run) to "indeterminate". A most-recent-run test
#      needs at least one verdict that actually differs between the two runs;
#      the 16:00 run's kadaster classes verdict is unchanged: "verified".
#   4. Kadaster's content sample in this (20:00) run has one sampledValue
#      swapped: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction> (present in the
#      16:00 run's kadaster sample) is replaced by
#      <urn:sparqlwatch:test:new-scheme-only-class>, which appears nowhere
#      else in this file. This makes "which run's sample is returned"
#      testable the same way run-two-sweeps.nq's CURRENT_ONLY_CLASS /
#      STALE_ONLY_CLASS pair makes it testable there.
#
# NEW_RUN = urn:sparqlwatch:run:2026-08-22T20:00:00Z (new subject scheme, most
#   recent).
# OLD_RUN = urn:sparqlwatch:run:2026-08-22T16:00:00Z (old subject scheme,
#   from run-with-samples.nq, older).
# NEW_SCHEME_CLASSES_VERDICT = "indeterminate": kadaster's sw:metric:classes
#   value in NEW_RUN.
# OLD_SCHEME_CLASSES_VERDICT = "verified": kadaster's sw:metric:classes value
#   in OLD_RUN.
# NEW_SCHEME_ONLY_CLASS = <urn:sparqlwatch:test:new-scheme-only-class>:
#   present in NEW_RUN's kadaster sample only.
# OLD_SCHEME_ONLY_CLASS = <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>:
#   present in OLD_RUN's kadaster sample only.
#
# A query answering kadaster's verdicts and content, with both runs loaded,
# must return NEW_RUN's values (NEW_SCHEME_CLASSES_VERDICT,
# NEW_SCHEME_ONLY_CLASS present, OLD_SCHEME_ONLY_CLASS absent), because
# 20:00 is the most recent run regardless of which subject scheme it uses.
# OLD_RUN must still be independently queryable: it is not deleted, only
# outranked.
